Package: sp9
Architecture: all
Depends:
 sp9-platform (= ${binary:Version}),
 sp9-helper (>= ${binary:Version}),
 sp9-digitizerd,
 ${misc:Depends},
Recommends:
 sp9-settings,
 sp9-dkms,
 sp9-cmdline,
Suggests:
 sp9-dkms-bluetooth,
 sp9-libcamera,
Description: Surface Pro 9 (Intel) support on top of linux-surface
 Installs the pieces that make the Microsoft Surface Pro 9 with an Intel CPU
 (SKU Surface_Pro_9_2038) work on top of the linux-surface kernel: the
 platform files, the device helper and the touch and pen daemon sp9-digitizerd,
 which replaces linux-surface's iptsd. It recommends the kernel modules of this
 project (sp9-dkms), the settings app and the kernel command line. This is a
 metapackage: it holds no files of its own. To keep iptsd, install the other
 sp9 packages without this one.

Package: sp9-helper
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 dbus-system-bus | dbus,
 polkitd,
 python3,
Recommends:
 kmod,
 pciutils,
 usbutils,
Suggests:
 sp9-settings,
 alsa-utils,
 alsa-tools,
 evtest,
 i2c-tools,
 libinput-tools,
 lm-sensors,
 v4l-utils,
Description: Surface Pro 9 (Intel) device helper (sp9-helperd, sp9-ctl)
 sp9-helperd is a system D-Bus service for the device-specific controls of
 the Surface Pro 9 with an Intel CPU: performance profiles with the Windows
 power limits, battery health and smart charging, panel self refresh policy,
 the panel colour profile, the Type Cover backlight, touch and pen settings,
 pen haptics and coupling, and a diagnostics export. Changes are authorized
 by polkit. sp9-ctl is its command-line client. The service starts only on
 this model (SMBIOS SKU Surface_Pro_9_2038). It reports the installed package
 versions and the state of the sp9-dkms kernel modules; it never downloads or
 installs anything itself.

Package: sp9-settings
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 sp9-helper,
Description: Surface Pro 9 (Intel) settings app
 A GTK 4 and libadwaita front-end for sp9-helperd: performance profiles,
 battery and smart charging, panel self refresh, Type Cover backlight, touch
 sensitivity, pen haptics and the diagnostics export.

Package: sp9-digitizerd
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 dbus-system-bus | dbus,
Conflicts:
 iptsd,
Description: Surface Pro 9 (Intel) touch and pen daemon
 sp9-digitizerd turns the raw data of the Surface Pro 9 digitizer (HID
 045E:0C52) into a touchscreen and a stylus through uinput. It is a port of
 iptsd with this project's pen processing, keeps its input devices across
 suspend and takes setting changes from sp9-helperd over D-Bus without a
 restart. It replaces iptsd: both read the same device, so only one of them
 can be installed.

Package: sp9-platform
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 iio-sensor-proxy,
Recommends:
 pipewire (>= 1.0),
 wireplumber (>= 0.5),
 swh-plugins,
Description: Surface Pro 9 (Intel) platform files
 Configuration files the Surface Pro 9 with an Intel CPU needs whatever the
 desktop: the iptsd preset and the libinput quirk for the pen's tip threshold,
 PSR1 only on the panel through i915 debugfs (no tainting kernel parameter),
 the udev rule that makes the accelerometer report at rest (for automatic
 rotation through iio-sensor-proxy), pinctrl_tigerlake in the initramfs (power
 and volume buttons), and the PipeWire and WirePlumber configuration for the
 speakers (protection filter chain, raw sink at 100 %), the microphones and an
 echo-cancelled microphone source.

Package: sp9-cmdline
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Enhances:
 grub2-common,
Description: Surface Pro 9 (Intel) kernel command line
 Adds the kernel parameters this project recommends for the Surface Pro 9 on
 the linux-surface kernel to GRUB through /etc/default/grub.d and runs
 update-grub. Removing the package removes them again. Other boot loaders: the
 parameters are in /usr/share/sp9-platform/cmdline.

Package: sp9-archive-keyring
Architecture: all
Build-Profiles: <!nokeyring>
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: OpenPGP key of the surface-pro-9-linux package repository
 The public key that signs the apt repository of surface-pro-9-linux, in
 /usr/share/keyrings/sp9-archive-keyring.gpg, for the Signed-By field of its
 sources entry. Updates of this package carry new or rotated keys.
